{"id": "EUVD-2026-102354", "enisaUuid": "811faec4-5c2f-34d1-bbfc-dabcef3c4905", "description": "FluidSynth through 2.6.1 contains an out-of-bounds write vulnerability that allows attackers to corrupt heap and stack memory by supplying unvalidated SoundFont modulator destination values. Attackers can craft an SF2 file with PMOD/IMOD destinations of 63 to 255 that, when loaded and played, write past the voice generator array and updated_gen_bit, causing memory corruption and crashes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:46:31", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/fluidsynth-sf2-modulator-dest-generator-oob-write", "https://github.com/FluidSynth/fluidsynth/blob/71e85b2ca6bf48641ba7e2261d8f2640ae473773/src/synth/fluid_voice.c#L615-L623", "https://github.com/FluidSynth/fluidsynth/blob/71e85b2ca6bf48641ba7e2261d8f2640ae473773/src/synth/fluid_voice.c#L1184-L1229", "https://github.com/FluidSynth/fluidsynth/blob/71e85b2ca6bf48641ba7e2261d8f2640ae473773/src/sfloader/fluid_defsfont.c#L1609-L1611", "https://github.com/FluidSynth/fluidsynth", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/fluidsynth-through-2.6.1-out-of-bounds-write-via-soundfont-modulator-destination"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111123", "GHSA-7hc9-ggv2-4w8c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "52f2c510-5b9e-3e01-b183-d9b60fa3b145", "product": {"name": "fluidsynth", "vendor": {"name": "FluidSynth"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.6.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "48b36c9e-933e-30be-9d07-8c7bcfc1ce4c", "vendor": {"name": "FluidSynth"}}], "isExploited": false}